          "Two fields often settle a cash forecast account: does the origin match the system, and does the named approver still hold that authority? The forecast line entry should name the field that changed, not just the fact that something changed. A dated observation is worth more than a current screenshot that cannot show what the entry said earlier.",
          "Missing, unavailable, and confirmed negative values belong in separate fields. The entry should let the next reviewer see which parts were checked and which were assumed. Every forecast line needs an observation time, because a later reader cannot infer it from context."
