        "heading": "The daily cash forecast routine",
        "paragraphs": [
          "A five-minute end-of-shift note prevents most next-morning confusion. The forecast review should be cleared of duplicate entries before new work starts. Log the exception where the next person will look, not in a private note. A routine that fits on one page is more likely to survive a busy week. For this step, the written action is to route any material gap to the finance owner.",
          "The analyst should leave each forecast line with a date and a next step. Review the cash forecast list before accepting a new request, not after. A consistent daily start time makes the queue easier to trust.",
          "The daily cash forecast routine is short: open the list, confirm the origin, log the exception, and leave a named next action. Start with the oldest unresolved item, because age turns a small gap into an escalation. Small habits carry cash forecast: date the origin, initial the check, state the next action, and never copy a familiar value."
        ]
